   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/Probability/Moments/Basic.lean:125 `def cgf (X : \u03a9 \u2192 \u211d) (\u03bc : Measure \u03a9) (t : \u211d) : \u211d := log (mgf X \u03bc t)`. Mathlib's own cgf lemmas always reduce the log (`cgf_gaussianReal` \u2192 `\u03bc * t + v * t ^ 2 / 2` at Gaussian/Real.lean:510; `cgf_const` \u2192 `t * c` at Moments/Basic.lean:158), as does this repo's `Probability.cgf_id_chiSquaredMeasure` \u2192 `-(k / 2) * Real.log (1 - 2 * t)` (code/TauCeti/Probability/Distributions/ChiSquared.lean:325).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Probability/Distributions/Gaussian/QuadraticForm.lean",
   "fix": "State the cgf in reduced form, e.g. `cgf ... t = -(1/2) * Real.log (1 - (2*t) \u2022 (\u0398 * S)).det` (and the `\u221aS` analogue), proved by `rw [cgf, mgf_..., Real.log_rpow ht.det_pos]` \u2014 `Matrix.PosDef.det_pos` is at mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/Matrix/PosDef.lean:85 and `Real.log_rpow` at mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Pow/Real.lean:494; for the `\u0398 * S` version transfer positivity through `PosSemidef.det_one_sub_smul_sqrt_mul_mul_sqrt`. If the reduced form is not wanted, drop both lemmas and let callers use the mgf lemmas with `cgf`.",
   "issue": "`cgf_inner_toEuclideanLin_multivariateGaussian_sqrt` (line 228) and `cgf_inner_toEuclideanLin_multivariateGaussian` (line 248) state `cgf ... = Real.log (det ... ^ (-1/2))` and are proved by `rw [cgf, <the mgf lemma>]`. Since `cgf X \u03bc t` is *defined* as `log (mgf X \u03bc t)` (mathlib/Mathlib/Probability/Moments/Basic.lean:125-126), these are `congrArg Real.log` applied to `mgf_inner_toEuclideanLin_multivariateGaussian_sqrt` / `mgf_inner_toEuclideanLin_multivariateGaussian` and add no content over them.",
   "line": "228"
  }
 ],
